(* Phase 11b G1 (s183) — chain-integrable sibling of the combined cut above, *)
(* WITHOUT the `read X12 = word_zx sx12` precondition.                        *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* The cut above keeps an X12 entry precondition (mirroring                   *)
(* HTABLE_KMID_FLAG_X12_INV's interface), but X12's entry value is DEAD: the  *)
(* kernel recomputes X12 at offset 0x64 (`lsr x12, x11, #32`) before any read,*)
(* so the X12 self-reference POST holds regardless of the entry value.  This  *)
(* matters for chain integration: at the prelude chain's s21 (PC=0x54) the    *)
(* X12 register is UNCONSTRAINED (PT_BODY's PRE asserts no X12 entry fact), so *)
(* binding the above cut's `sx12 := word_subword (read X12 s21) (0,32)` would  *)
(* leave an unprovable residual `read X12 s21 =                               *)
(* word_zx (word_subword (read X12 s21) (0,32))`.  Dropping the X12 PRE here   *)
(* avoids that: at PC=0x244 the X12 value IS `word_zx Z` (Z:int32), so the     *)
(* self-ref POST closes via `MATCH_MP_TAC EQ_SYM` + the word_zx/word_subword   *)
(* helper.  Everything else is identical to the cut above.                    *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* This is the form that AES_GCM_MAIN_LOOP_PRELUDE_PRE_FIRSTBLOCKS_FLAG_X5_   *)
