(* Phase 11b G1 (s184) — PT_BODY clone exposing Q0..Q3 in AES spec form.      *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Clone of AES_GCM_MAIN_LOOP_PRELUDE_PRE_FIRSTBLOCKS_FLAG_X5_X12_PT_BODY_    *)
(* CORRECT (above) whose POST additionally asserts the four AES outputs       *)
(*   read Qi s = aese (aes_arm_round^9                                        *)
(*                       (word_bytereverse (aes_gcm_ctr_at                    *)
(*                          (word_bytereverse ctr0) i)) [rk0..rk8]) rk9       *)
(* for i = 0..3 — the ciphertext-keystream blocks in AES spec form, the      *)
(* G1 ciphertext bridge's left-hand side.                                    *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Three changes vs. the original BODY_CORRECT:                               *)
(*   - PRE adds rk4 (@[key_ptr,#64]) and rk8 (@[key_ptr,#128]) memory facts   *)
(*     (the combined cut needs all of rk0..rk8) and one nonoverlap antecedent *)
(*     nonoverlapping (word pc, ...) (key_ptr, 256).                          *)
(*   - The inline ARM_STEPS(22--60) + HTABLE_KMID_FLAG_X12_INV cut over       *)
(*     0xf0..0x244 is replaced by a single MP of the combined                 *)
(*     AES_GCM_PRELUDE_HTABLE_KMID_FLAG_BLOCK0123_NOX12_CORRECT cut over       *)
(*     instr 22..145 (0x54..0x244), which carries the Q0..Q3 AES form.       *)
(*   - POST adds the four Q0..Q3 AES-form conjuncts.                          *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Two close subtleties (see [[g1_combined_prelude_cut]]):                    *)
(*   - sx5 is bound to the CONCRETE X5 value at s21 (word_sub byte_len 1),   *)
(*     NOT `read X5 s21`: the cut's X5 POST must not reference an old state    *)
(*     or DISCARD_OLDSTATE drops it after ARM_BIGSTEP.                        *)
(*   - ARM_BIGSTEP leaves the cut's PRE conjunct ctr0 = word_join ctr_hi      *)
(*     ctr_lo as a side subgoal, discharged via READ_MEMORY_BYTESIZED_SPLIT  *)
(*     against the three s21 ivec memory reads.                              *)
