(* ==========================================================================
 * Phase 10 (s127) — Path (c) Step 5: body-only per-N whole-kernel wrappers.
 *
 * Body versions of the existing per-N (N=1/2/3/4) wrappers
 * (`AES_GCM_ENC_KERNEL_BYTE_LEN_LE_{16,32,48,64_4}_CORRECT` at lines
 * 26269/26467/26650/26846).  Each body version:
 *
 *   - Replaces `MP_TAC AES_GCM_MAIN_LOOP_PRELUDE_N0_KERNEL_CORRECT` with
 *     `MP_TAC AES_GCM_MAIN_LOOP_PRELUDE_N0_BODY_KERNEL_CORRECT` (s126
 *     Step 4, line 25960).
 *   - PRE.PC shifts from `word pc` to `word (pc + 0x2c)`.
 *   - PRE.SP shifts from `stackpointer` to `word_sub stackpointer (word 128)`.
 *   - Adds `read X16 s = ivec_ptr` and `read X8 s = key_ptr` to PRE
 *     (PRELUDE_N0_BODY's PRE requires these; the prologue established
 *     them in the original PRELUDE_N0).
 *   - Drops SP, X8, X16, X29 from MAYCHANGE (none written by body).
 *   - Drops `bytes(stackpointer-128, 128)` spill-stack atom from MAYCHANGE
 *     (body doesn't touch the stack).
 *   - Drops the four stack-related nonoverlap clauses + `aligned 16
 *     stackpointer` from antecedents (no longer relevant for body-only).
 *
 * TAIL_N{1,2,3,4}_FULL_{,CLOSED_}KERNEL_CORRECT wrappers reused as-is —
 * they don't reference SP in PRE/POST and are SP-agnostic.
 *
 * Closing residuals identical to the original wrappers' closing
 * residuals (X12 self-ref + IVAL_EQ_VAL bridge).
