(* Session 177 — LE_64 CLOSED (tag-anchored) functional unifier.              *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* Unifies the 4 tag-ANCHORED LE-path CLOSED wrappers                         *)
(* (AES_GCM_ENC_KERNEL_BYTE_LEN_{LE_16,LE_32,LE_48,LE_64_4}_BODY_FUNCTIONAL_  *)
(*  CLOSED_CORRECT @39248/40147/40542/40958) into a single byte_len band      *)
(* dispatch.  Differs from the un-anchored LE_64 unifier (@41369) in:         *)
(*   - extra universal binder `initial_tag:int128`;                           *)
(*   - PRE conjunct `read (memory :> bytes128 xiptr) s = initial_tag`         *)
(*     (anchors the GHASH initial tag to the input Xi buffer);                *)
(*   - POST per-band existentials use the ANCHORED running tag                 *)
(*     `nist_ghash h (word_bytereverse initial_tag) [...]` (NOT a free        *)
(*     `?prev_tag`).  Hence a non-vacuous functional statement.               *)
(*                                                                            *)
(* This is the genuine precursor for the byte_list_at presentation theorem    *)
(* (C5/C6) for the byte_len <= 64 band.                                       *)
